<p>When I reviewed this, I said something about the disconcerting nature of the unknown. That unsettling feeling when you see preparations being made, but aren't given an explanation as to why.</p>
<p>The setup to this is astoundingly large in scale. Evacuating the entire eastern seaboard, activating SCP-2000, preparing for a 250 year long rebuilding process, but then very little in the way of <em>why</em>. The logs are vague, the explanations are vague, everything leads towards something nasty without outright saying it. And that's spooky.</p>
<p>There's enough here to leave me unsettled. I don't think this is perfect, conceptually, but it does more than enough to give me pause. I'll be thinking about it for a while.</p>

